{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "label": "Spectral Anti-Fraud Check \u2014 FFT cutoff (brick-wall) detector, v1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Detects MP3s/AAC transcoded up to FLAC \u2014 the most common Soulseek fraud \u2014 by finding the brick-wall low-pass fingerprint the original lossy encoder imprinted; applies only to P2P-sourced files claiming lossless quality (D3); pure-numpy STFT with async ffmpeg pipe keeps the whole phase \u22643 s per file."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_spectral_py", "label": "analysis/spectral.py (normative target of docs/04)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_decision_d3", "label": "Decision D3 \u2014 only P2P lossless-claiming files are spectrally checked", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fallback streams have known lossy provenance (Opus 128\u2013160k is full-band to \u224820 kHz with no brick-wall cliff), so there is no fraud signal to detect; exempting them avoids wasted analysis on files whose provenance is already honest."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_mp3_upcast_fraud", "label": "Threat (a) \u2014 MP3/AAC \u2192 FLAC upcast", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Primary v1 target: hard spectral cutoff at the encoder lowpass (\u224816 kHz @128k, \u224818\u201319 kHz @192k, \u224820\u201320.5 kHz @320k LAME) with a very steep cliff; accepted limitation \u2014 a 320k MP3 upcast cuts at \u224820.5 kHz and passes v1 rules, but is audibly near-transparent; strictness is tunable."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_hires_upsample_fraud", "label": "Threat (b) \u2014 44.1 kHz \u2192 96/192 kHz upsample (hi-res void)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Content void above 22.05 kHz despite a hi-res claim; v1 emits a soft INCONCLUSIVE flag (rule 5), full FRAUD rule deferred to v2 \u00a79."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_fake_bitdepth_fraud", "label": "Threat (c) \u2014 16-bit \u2192 fake 24-bit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_verdict_rules", "label": "Verdict rules v1 (FRAUD / INCONCLUSIVE / PASS), evaluation order", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "False-positive containment: steepness gates (f_c \u2264 19 kHz with S \u2265 30 dB/kHz etc.) protect legitimately band-limited recordings (historical transfers, gradual-rolloff classical/mastered content); cost asymmetry \u2014 a rare false FRAUD costs one re-download via fallback while a false PASS admits a fake-lossless file \u2014 so thresholds deliberately favor rejection within the cliff-evidence regime."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_spectral_strict", "label": "spectral.strict config flag", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Default: INCONCLUSIVE treated as PASS with a WARNING (lazy pass); when spectral.strict = true an INCONCLUSIVE verdict triggers the fallback instead \u2014 trading warned-passes for re-downloads when a lossless claim is doubtful."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_fixture_suite", "label": "Test fixture suite (7 fixtures, scipy/soundfile recipes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deviation note (M4): the original Butterworth order-8 recipe rolled off only \u224815 dB at 4 kHz above a 16 kHz cutoff (48 dB/octave) vs the DEAD_MARGIN_DB = 55 rule, drifting to false PASS; real lossy encoders brick-wall (spectrum above cutoff is encoded to zero), so fixtures now use a deterministic raised-cosine mask with a 500 Hz transition band and a hard zero knee. \u00a76 thresholds were not changed; tuning protocol: adjust \u00a76 thresholds, never fixture recipes."}, {"id": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_q_spectral", "label": "q_spectral worker queue (one worker, \u224820 files/min)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_spectral_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_decision_d3", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_mp3_upcast_fraud", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_hires_upsample_fraud", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_fake_bitdepth_fraud", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_verdict_rules", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_spectral_strict", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_q_spectral", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_check", "target": "readme_ffmpeg", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_verdict_rules", "target": "readme_decision_d12", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/04-spectral-antifraud.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_04_spectral_antifraud_verdict_rules", "target": "readme_docs_03_pipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": 